# SysML Parallel TVCache — project agent rules

Teammate-facing docs: root `README.md` only. Exp A evidence: single `docs/workload_characterization_report.md` (add a table row per new cell). Experiments A/B/C via `bash scripts/run_experiment.sh {none|sequential|parallel|all}` (only `none` implemented today; mode picks one experiment unless `all`). Exp B sequential TVCache can proceed in parallel (stub until tvclient wired).

## Deployment boundaries

- NERSC is inference-only. Harbor / Pi / task / verifier run on the Mac via Docker.
- Use only m4999 (`--account=m4999 --constraint=gpu`). Never ntrain5.
- Proven A0 alloc: 1 GPU, 32 CPUs, 56G, `shared_interactive`. A1: 4 GPUs, TP=4, ~220G, often `interactive` QOS. Preferred later 9B serve: **2 GPUs / TP=2**, ~120G, `interactive` (A2 TP2 pilot). Release promptly; `scancel` on backend death or Mac runner stall.
- FlashInfer workaround until retested: node-local JIT caches + `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0`.
- Valid vLLM flag: `--default-chat-template-kwargs`. Qwen3.5 text DeepSWE: `--language-model-only` (+ `--reasoning-parser qwen3` when thinking off).
- Live runs need fresh MFA: `sshproxy -u <user> -f` (browser / Iris federated login). Prefer Terminal.app / `screen -dmS … bash scripts/…` over Cursor-shell `nohup` (Cursor can reap the process group while orphan Docker/Slurm keep going).
- Harbor Pi custom endpoint needs host env `OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:18081/v1` + `OPENAI_API_KEY=EMPTY` (set in `run_harbor_wave.sh`). Omitting it yields `model_api requires an explicitly configured base URL` and zero sessions — quarantine those job dirs and re-run.
- Resume a live NERSC serve with `SYSML_ATTACH_JOB` + `SYSML_ATTACH_NODE` (after `bridge_up` is defined). Do not `scancel` a READY alloc just because the Mac runner died.
- Default wave: `SYSML_PASS_K=5`, `SYSML_HARBOR_N=5`, `SYSML_MAX_NUM_SEQS=5`, `SYSML_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80`, tasks from `configs/experiment-tasks.txt` (10 setup variants). Recycle alloc every `SYSML_TASKS_PER_ALLOC` (default 2). GPU monitor: `scripts/monitor_nersc_gpu.sh` / `gpu-monitor.log`.
- Do not confuse knobs: `SYSML_MAX_MODEL_LEN` / `SYSML_CONTEXT_WINDOW` = total prompt+history capacity; `SYSML_MAX_TOKENS` = **per-completion** generation cap; `SYSML_MAX_TURNS` = assistant **turn** ceiling (not tokens). Reward 0 + turn exhaustion ≠ “ran out of 256K context.”
- DeepSWE/TMax = **task suites**; Pi/Mini-SWE = **harnesses**; Harbor = orchestrator. Exp A DeepSWE reward 0 = task hardness. **T1/T2** = same **Harbor+Pi**, TMax tasks: T1 5/5; T2 **40/40** on 8 valid (exclude `001033` env-timeout, `009942` agent-timeout). Natural Pi only. Not Exp B TVCache.
- Handout Tables 1–2 in root `README.md` use explicit matched contract: Harbor+Pi · Qwen3.8-27B · 8 ids in `experiment-tasks-tmax-easy8.txt` · pass@5/n=5 · 256K/100 turns/xhigh/TP4. DeepSWE Table 1 row = A3; TVCache rows TBD until Exp B/C.
- Wave `manifest.json` `purpose` follows `SYSML_TASK_ROOT` (tmax vs deep-swe). Analyzer `--benchmark` defaults to the string `DeepSWE` — tag only; pass `--benchmark TMax` for T* summaries.

## Evidence honesty

- Reward 0 + `exception_info=null` is graded unsuccessful, not infra success by itself.
- Inspect Pi session + verifier; do not invent rewards or manufacture parallelism.
- Preserve `jobs/` / `results/` evidence. Never commit `.local-smoke/` or `.env`.

## Characterization

- Handout Experiment A uses `variants/deep-swe-setup/` (setup in instruction). Do not edit `vendor/deep-swe/tasks/` in place.
- Parallel-turn fraction = turns with >1 emitted call / all assistant turns (incl. zero-call).
- Analyze with `bash scripts/analyze_characterization_wave.sh <prefix>` — do not glob unrelated `jobs/`.
- TVCache key = trajectory prefix in the TCG. Paper win = cross-rollout reuse (Exp B). Within-turn N>1 is Exp C.
- Forced-parallel stress (`MultitoolPi` / `SYSML_PARALLEL_STRESS` / `--parallel-test`, PR #1) is **not** Exp A natural rate. Cite `docs/parallel_prompt_stress_report.md` separately. Soft prompt (“parallel when appropriate”) for ≥27B; hard “AS MANY” only for emission stress. Exp C also needs **cache hits on parallel-tool turns**, not just parallel-turn %.
- When the goal is **solve + parallel stress**, keep proven capability knobs (27B: **4 GPU / TP=4 / 256K / 250 turns / k=5**). Do not cut context/turns just to fit 2 GPUs — allocate more GPUs instead.
- DeepSWE (even “easy” happy-dom) stays reward 0 on Qwen3.8-27B pass@5 — too hard for capability demos. Prefer **TMax short+bash-only** tasks for solve-rate smoke (`variants/tmax-easy/`, `configs/experiment-tasks-tmax-easy1.txt`). Harbor registry `tmax/…` needs `harbor auth login`; local extract from HF `TMaxxx/TMax-15K-Harbor` `tasks.zip` works with `-p`.
- Parallel-turn metric = **model-emitted** >1 tool_call in one assistant message (not wall-clock overlap). Mini-SWE **does** accept multi-`bash` in one turn (B1: 84/378, always n=2); default agent executes them **sequentially** (`for action in actions`). Stock Harbor mini prompt does not push MULTIPLE; Qwen3.8-27B still emitted pairs. `analyze_characterization_wave.py` only reads Pi `*.jsonl` — Mini-SWE needs ATIF / `mini-swe-agent.trajectory.json`.

## Model / runner sync

- When changing model id, update sbatch, gateway `--model`, `SYSML_MODEL_ID`, LoopbackPi, and Harbor `-m` together.
- Harbor agent: **default Pi** (`LoopbackPi`) for Exp A/B/C + TVCache (`tvclient` on Pi tool-execute). Mini-SWE (`LoopbackMiniSwe`) is optional isolation only — also emits multi-tool turns but bash-only, sequential exec, weaker analyzer/TVCache fit. Do not switch primary harness for parallel emission alone.
- Harbor 0.24 mini-swe install needs `--with mcp` (litellm tools path); local patch on `uv tool` harbor until upgrade pulls main's `litellm[mcp]`. Re-apply after `uv tool upgrade harbor`.
- Active pilot model: `Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B` (tool parser `qwen3_coder`); B2 uses `Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8`. Prior Exp A cells remain `Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B`.
- Qwen3.8 reasoning effort ≠ 9B: vLLM rejects `high`. Use Harbor `SYSML_THINKING` ∈ `xhigh`|`medium`|`low` only.
- Live Harbor waves need the **Mac awake** (tunnel + Docker). Laptop sleep → stop Mac wave + `scancel` interactive GPU jobs; NERSC CPU downloads (e.g. `sysml-hf-flash`) can keep going.
- Kill a stuck Mac wave with `kill -9` on the wave/harbor PIDs if you must preserve a READY NERSC alloc — bash `EXIT` trap in `run_harbor_wave.sh` runs `scancel`.
- Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8 on Perlmutter A100 (SM80): Triton/DeepGEMM FP8 MoE need SM≥8.9. Try `--moe-backend marlin` (+ often `--enable-expert-parallel`); plain TP4+triton fails. Official recipe is Hopper H100/H200 TEP.
